//
//  Local.xcconfig.example
//
//  Copy this file to Config/Local.xcconfig (which Git ignores) to sign with your own
//  free "Apple Development" certificate (a Personal Team) instead of ad hoc.
//  A stable identity keeps the permissions macOS gave the app (Files and Folders) from
//  one build to the next, which an ad hoc signature, different at every build, does not.
//
//  Put your own values here and never commit this file: no team ID, certificate or
//  e-mail belongs in the repository.
//
//  Find your Team ID in Xcode > Settings > Accounts > your Apple ID > Personal Team,
//  or with:  security find-identity -v -p codesigning
//
//  This file is a template: its lines are commented out until you uncomment them.
//

// CODE_SIGN_STYLE = Automatic
// CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY = Apple Development
// DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = YOURTEAMID
// ENABLE_HARDENED_RUNTIME = YES
// OTHER_CODE_SIGN_FLAGS =
